        "rendered_user_prompt": "List every meeting date proposed in the request below.\n\n<request>\nsHPMJphrkkguSXDmJcGF\n</request>\n\n---\nThe instance we want to generate will be for the following class:\nclass DateContent(StuffContent):\n    \"\"\"A calendar date, optionally with a time of day — as precise as its source states.\n\n    The optional ``time`` carries the UTC offset on its ``tzinfo`` when the source states one\n    (fidelity, not normalization). Invalid states are unrepresentable by construction: no time\n    without a date, no offset without a time.\n    \"\"\"\n    date: date  # The calendar date, in ISO 8601 (e.g. 2026-07-07). Always required.\n    time: time | None = None  # The time of day, in ISO 8601 (e.g. 15:40:00, or 15:40:00+02:00 with a UTC offset). Include it only when the source states a time — never invent a time. Keep the UTC offset exactly when the source states one.\n\nDO NOT create information.\nIf some information is not present for an attribute, output the default value or None according to the attribute definition.",
